From b2cb6d1a3f36d661a32d4339c6a5cabda8157a32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sds-elastic build <sds-elastic@flant.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Bump Go dependencies with known CVEs

Rook v1.19.5 pins several modules at versions with fixed CVEs. They are
all linked into the rook binary this image ships, so the module CVE gate
reports them against the released image:

  github.com/moby/spdystream  0.5.0 -> 0.5.1   CVE-2026-35469
  golang.org/x/crypto        0.45.0 -> 0.53.0  CVE-2026-39827/39828/39829/
                                               39830/39831/39832/39833/
                                               39834/39835/42508/46595/
                                               46597/46598
  golang.org/x/net           0.47.0 -> 0.56.0  CVE-2026-25680/25681/27136/
                                               33814/39821/42502/42506/
                                               46600
  golang.org/x/sys           0.38.0 -> 0.46.0  CVE-2026-39824
  golang.org/x/text          0.31.0 -> 0.39.0  CVE-2026-56852

All of them are indirect dependencies, so only their minimums move;
go mod tidy carried the x/sync and x/term minimums along. pkg/apis is a
separate module (replaced locally by the root go.mod) and is bumped in
step so both module graphs agree and a filesystem scan of the source tree
is clean too.

No source change - go.mod/go.sum only. Drop this patch once the pinned
Rook release ships the bumps itself.
---
 go.mod          | 14 +++++++-------
 go.sum          | 36 ++++++++++++++++++------------------
 pkg/apis/go.mod |  9 ++++-----
 pkg/apis/go.sum | 28 ++++++++++++++--------------
 4 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 44 deletions(-)

